e of the chessboard (n), ChessSize.\n\nConstraints:\n\n1 <= n <= 250\n\nOutput Format:\n\nPrint the number of valid moves.\n\nSample Test Case 1:\n\nInput:\n\n2\n2\n2\n4\n4\n\nOutput:\n\n4\n\nExplanation:\n\nFro", "author_tag": "IITD", "reply_to": {"id": 21855, "text": "infoedge questions please ?", "author_tag": "BHU"}, "attachment": null, "deleted": false}
